      "solution": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void)\n{\n    unsigned int n, k;\n    scanf(\"%u\", &n);\n    scanf(\"%u\", &k);\n\n    unsigned int x = n ^ k;\n    unsigned int encrypted = ((x << 1) | (x >> 7)) & 255;\n\n    printf(\"%u\\n\", encrypted);\n    return 0;\n}",
      "statement": "You are given an {{8}}-bit unsigned integer [[n]] and an {{8}}-bit key [[k]].\n\nEncrypt [[n]] using the following two operations:\n\n1. Compare the bits of [[n]] and [[k]] using the <<XOR>> logic gate.\n2. Rotate the resulting {{8}} bits one position to the left.\n\nThe leftmost bit wraps around to become the rightmost bit.\n\nOutput the encrypted value as a decimal integer.",
