    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">You are given an <const>8</const>-bit unsigned integer <var>n</var> and an <const>8</const>-bit key <var>k</var>.<br><br>Encrypt <var>n</var> using the following two operations:<br><br>1. Compare the bits of <var>n</var> and <var>k</var> using the <strong>XOR</strong> logic gate.<br>2. Rotate the resulting <const>8</const> bits one position to the left.<br><br>The leftmost bit wraps around to become the rightmost bit.<br><br>Output the encrypted value as a decimal integer.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> An integer <var>n</var>.<br><strong>Line 2:</strong> An integer <var>k</var>.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> The encrypted value as a decimal integer.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">0 &le; <var>n</var> &le; 255<br>0 &le; <var>k</var> &le; 255</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">42\n15</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">74</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
